section.body:
**R-1 — Complete source-backed feature census.**
```requirement
{
  "intent": {
    "request": "Enumerate the exposed hosted cloud and GCP/AWS BYOC journeys, supported environments, route writers, dependencies, current acceptance evidence, and resource cleanup. Every census entry must have an assigned scenario and explicit result; unsupported provider options must fail closed rather than appear validated."
  },
  "acceptance": {
    "condition": "Enumerate the exposed hosted cloud and GCP/AWS BYOC journeys, supported environments, route writers, dependencies, current acceptance evidence, and resource cleanup. Every census entry must have an assigned scenario and explicit result; unsupported provider options must fail closed rather than appear validated.",
    "falsifier": "A documented supported cloud journey, provider/runtime, required failure path or resource obligation has no scenario/result entry."
  },
  "verification": {
    "method": "Inspect current hosted/BYOC route and UI writers; enumerate every documented cloud journey/provider/runtime in the P-001 scenario census, partition each into checked/notChecked/notApplicable, and verify each has test and cleanup evidence or an owned gap.",
    "check": {
      "kind": "instrument",
      "instrumentKey": "none"
    }
  }
}
```

**R-2 — Persistent end-to-end coverage.**
```requirement
{
  "intent": {
    "request": "Cover sign-in and organization/workspace admission; setup and provider credential validation; configure and cost review; provision to healthy connection; launch and complete an agent task; desktop/browser interaction; stop/start and reconnect; snapshot and restore; repair and failed provisioning; billing/entitlements; tutorial pause/resume; destroy and resource accounting. Add missing regression scenarios in the project's actual test frameworks and affected-suite routing."
  },
  "acceptance": {
    "condition": "Cover sign-in and organization/workspace admission; setup and provider credential validation; configure and cost review; provision to healthy connection; launch and complete an agent task; desktop/browser interaction; stop/start and reconnect; snapshot and restore; repair and failed provisioning; billing/entitlements; tutorial pause/resume; destroy and resource accounting. Add missing regression scenarios in the project's actual test frameworks and affected-suite routing.",
    "falsifier": "A supported happy-path journey lacks a persistent passing end-to-end or integration guard, or the affected suite does not select it.",
    "requiredTestLayers": [
      "unit",
      "integration",
      "e2e"
    ]
  },
  "verification": {
    "method": "Run canonical API lifecycle tests and the real-component Cloud first-agent browser journey; inspect the resulting ledger rows, traces and affected-suite selection. Extend these suites for uncovered population entries.",
    "check": {
      "kind": "tests",
      "files": [
        "packages/operator-core/lib/endpoint-route/routes/workspace-hosts/connection.test.ts",
        "packages/operator-core/lib/endpoint-route/routes/workspace-hosts/provision.test.ts",
        "packages/operator-core/lib/endpoint-route/routes/workspace-hosts/action.test.ts",
        "apps/operator/e2e/cloud-tutorial.spec.ts",
        "packages/operator-core/lib/workspace-host/provisioning-runner.integration.test.ts",
        "packages/operator-core/lib/workspace-host/lifecycle-runner.restore.integration.test.ts"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

**R-3 — Adversarial and recovery acceptance.**
```requirement
{
  "intent": {
    "request": "Verify unauthorized access, tenant/workspace switching, stale credentials, delayed or failed operations, retries and duplicate submission, idempotence, reload/reconnect, unavailable provider and transport, redaction, keyboard/accessibility, and cleanup after partial failure. Distinguish real provider outcomes from mocked HTTP or fake-provider coverage."
  },
  "acceptance": {
    "condition": "Verify unauthorized access, tenant/workspace switching, stale credentials, delayed or failed operations, retries and duplicate submission, idempotence, reload/reconnect, unavailable provider and transport, redaction, keyboard/accessibility, and cleanup after partial failure. Distinguish real provider outcomes from mocked HTTP or fake-provider coverage.",
    "falsifier": "An unauthorized/duplicate/stale operation succeeds, recovery loses state, secrets leak, or a required failure/recovery scenario remains untested.",
    "requiredTestLayers": [
      "unit",
      "integration",
      "e2e"
    ]
  },
  "verification": {
    "method": "Execute isolation, unauthorized access, failure/retry, chaos and UI reload/permission scenarios; include at least one negative control per permission/lifecycle boundary and inspect sensitive output redaction.",
    "check": {
      "kind": "tests",
      "files": [
        "packages/operator-core/lib/workspace-host/lifecycle-runner.chaos.test.ts",
        "packages/operator-core/lib/workspace-host/hosted-lifecycle-policy.test.ts",
        "packages/operator-core/lib/endpoint-route/routes/workspace-hosts/action.test.ts",
        "apps/operator/e2e/cloud-tutorial.spec.ts",
        "packages/operator-core/lib/workspace-host/provisioning-runner.integration.test.ts",
        "packages/operator-core/lib/workspace-host/lifecycle-runner.restore.integration.test.ts"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

**R-4 — Verified durable repairs.**
```requirement
{
  "intent": {
    "request": "For each discovered in-scope defect, register and own the repair, isolate the root cause with differing predictions, fix the originating layer, add a recurrence guard, and re-run the affected journey. Out-of-scope residue must have an accountable owner."
  },
  "acceptance": {
    "condition": "For each discovered in-scope defect, register and own the repair, isolate the root cause with differing predictions, fix the originating layer, add a recurrence guard, and re-run the affected journey. Out-of-scope residue must have an accountable owner.",
    "falsifier": "A confirmed defect is closed without originating-layer fix, recurrence guard and passing triggering journey, or residue lacks an accountable assignee.",
    "requiredTestLayers": [
      "unit",
      "integration"
    ]
  },
  "verification": {
    "method": "For each defect inspect its work-item rootCauseVerification and originating source diff, execute its registered regression before/after and rerun the triggering scenario; verify residue assignees and cleanup obligations.",
    "check": {
      "kind": "tests",
      "files": [
        "packages/operator-core/lib/workspace-host/lifecycle-runner.test.ts",
        "packages/operator-core/lib/workspace-host/credential-lifecycle-runner.test.ts",
        "packages/operator-core/lib/workspace-host/teardown-release-receipt.test.ts",
        "packages/operator-core/lib/workspace-host/lifecycle-runner.restore.integration.test.ts"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

**R-5 — Real-runtime evidence.**
```requirement
{
  "intent": {
    "request": "Run maintained current-build routes for operator API, hosted/browser, desktop, and provider lifecycle. Use isolated test organizations/accounts/resources and uniquely tagged canaries; preserve exact source/artifact identities, commands, assertions, provider receipts, logs and teardown evidence. A skipped or unavailable scenario remains unverified and prevents a universal pass."
  },
  "acceptance": {
    "condition": "Run maintained current-build routes for operator API, hosted/browser, desktop, and provider lifecycle. Use isolated test organizations/accounts/resources and uniquely tagged canaries; preserve exact source/artifact identities, commands, assertions, provider receipts, logs and teardown evidence. A skipped or unavailable scenario remains unverified and prevents a universal pass.",
    "falsifier": "A real-runtime or provider result is inferred from mocks, identities differ, teardown is unproven, or a required supported runtime/provider path remains skipped."
  },
  "verification": {
    "method": "Use maintained isolated API/UI/native and real provider acceptance executors. Bind each result to source hash, served artifact, tenant/account and unique resource labels; inspect provider readiness, task completion, stop/start/snapshot/restore and destroy receipts. Retain evidence and separately flag mocks/skips.",
    "check": {
      "kind": "instrument",
      "instrumentKey": "none"
    }
  }
}
```

**R-6 — Exact shipped artifact.**
```requirement
{
  "intent": {
    "request": "After the applicable green promotion and deployment, verify cloud acceptance on the exact authenticated artifact serving the cloud app and applicable desktop/runtime artifact. Shipment requires the resulting source/artifact receipt, no unowned residue, a completion audit, plan-specific grading, and a verified owner report. Staging results alone do not meet this bar."
  },
  "acceptance": {
    "condition": "After the applicable green promotion and deployment, verify cloud acceptance on the exact authenticated artifact serving the cloud app and applicable desktop/runtime artifact. Shipment requires the resulting source/artifact receipt, no unowned residue, a completion audit, plan-specific grading, and a verified owner report. Staging results alone do not meet this bar.",
    "falsifier": "Plan is marked shipped from staging/fixture evidence, deployed artifact differs, final journey fails, or any required acceptance bar or owned residue remains unresolved."
  },
  "verification": {
    "method": "Read the authoritative exact deployed app/desktop artifact receipt and authenticated serving identity, execute final cloud smoke/journey acceptance on that artifact, verify promotion/deployment receipts, complete source audit/independent grading and report publication/readback.",
    "check": {
      "kind": "instrument",
      "instrumentKey": "none"
    }
  }
}
```
